# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

# START

Set current_room to "Front Door"

Display current room

Ask the player:

 "Enter a direction: North, South, East, or West"

Get the player's direction

IF current_room is "Front Door"

IF direction is East

Move to "Hallway"

ELSE:

Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE:

 IF current room is "Hallway"

IF direction is South

   Move to "Kitchen"

ELSE:

Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE:

IF current room is "Kitchen"

IF direction is East

Move to "Cellar"

ELSE:

Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE:

IF current room is "Cellar"

IF direction is South

Move to "Armory

 ELSE

 Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE 

IF current_room is "Armory"

IF direction is West

Move to "Award Room"

ELSE

        Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE IF current_room is "Award Room"

  IF direction is West

        Move to "Master Bedroom"

    ELSE

        Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE IF current_room is "Master Bedroom"

IF direction is South

        Move to "Stairwell"

    ELSE

        Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE IF current_room is "Stairwell"

IF direction is East

        Move  to "Dragon Dungeon"

    ELSE

        Display "You cannot go that way."

ELSE IF current_room is "Dragon Dungeon"

 Display "You have reached the dragon!"

END
